# Keep committed CSV artifacts byte-identical across platforms on checkout.
#
# The inventory CSV is evidence: reviewers compare a fresh run against the committed
# file. On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, git rewrites LF to CRLF in the
# working tree, and the comparison fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the
# inventory. Pinning eol=lf makes the checked-out bytes match the committed bytes
# everywhere.
#
# This is about the checkout side. autocrlf normalizes to LF at check-in, so it is not
# what produced the CRLF blob this replaces -- that came from the csv module's RFC-4180
# default line terminator, fixed in the writer itself.
*.csv text eol=lf
